00:45:29.760 --> 00:45:31.400
And I said, it's great, right?

00:45:31.400 --> 00:45:33.480
It's a great disguise.

00:45:33.480 --> 00:45:37.080
And he said, let's pull one on the ambassador.

00:45:37.080 --> 00:45:39.280
The ambassador I was working for was a dick.

00:45:39.280 --> 00:45:40.840
He's the only ambassador I ever worked for

00:45:40.840 --> 00:45:44.400
that I genuinely disliked and didn't respect.

00:45:44.400 --> 00:45:49.400
And so we walked in and the chief says, Mr. Ambassador,

00:45:49.840 --> 00:45:52.000
I wanted to introduce you to one of our experts

00:45:52.000 --> 00:45:53.600
in Washington, from Washington.

00:45:53.600 --> 00:45:55.800
This is Dr. So-and-so.

00:45:55.800 --> 00:45:57.760
And I said, how do you do, Mr. Ambassador?

00:45:57.760 --> 00:45:58.600
And he's like, how do you do?

00:45:58.600 --> 00:45:59.440
Please have a seat.

00:45:59.440 --> 00:46:03.240
And I sat down and we had a little chat, walked out.

00:46:03.240 --> 00:46:04.080
We didn't walk out.

00:46:04.080 --> 00:46:07.120
We walked to the door and I walked like this

00:46:07.120 --> 00:46:09.480
and I pulled the thing off.

00:46:10.960 --> 00:46:15.000
And he's like, I don't know how you guys live with yourselves.

00:46:16.680 --> 00:46:17.520
Yeah.

00:46:17.520 --> 00:46:18.860
And it was like, yeah.

00:46:18.860 --> 00:46:23.200
Oh my God, your life is so much more interesting

00:46:23.200 --> 00:46:25.720
than anyone's, I think.

00:46:25.720 --> 00:46:26.560
You know what?

00:46:26.560 --> 00:46:27.880
It's the life of a young man.

00:46:27.880 --> 00:46:30.120
I'm in my late fifties now.

00:46:30.120 --> 00:46:31.560
And this is all 30 years ago.

00:46:31.560 --> 00:46:33.200
I couldn't do this stuff anymore.

00:46:33.200 --> 00:46:34.720
Yeah, yeah.

00:46:34.720 --> 00:46:37.240
I would think you would have to have a,

00:46:37.280 --> 00:46:41.640
yeah, have to have a sort of that invincibility feeling

00:46:41.640 --> 00:46:43.280
about yourself to do it.

00:46:43.280 --> 00:46:44.600
Yeah, yeah.

00:46:44.600 --> 00:46:45.440
Right.

00:46:47.040 --> 00:46:49.560
You haven't realized you're mortal yet.

00:46:49.560 --> 00:46:50.880
Right, exactly.

00:46:50.880 --> 00:46:52.320
Yeah, exactly.

00:46:52.320 --> 00:46:56.320
That's, man, like I said, there is so much

00:46:56.320 --> 00:46:59.760
that I would love to hear you talk about.

00:46:59.760 --> 00:47:03.120
Since we're running kind of into the last little portion

00:47:03.120 --> 00:47:05.300
of what time you've got left though,

00:47:05.300 --> 00:47:09.980
if we can real quick maybe switch gears

00:47:09.980 --> 00:47:12.460
and kind of go into big picture.

00:47:12.460 --> 00:47:16.660
I just wanted to get your take on what's going on

00:47:16.660 --> 00:47:20.660
with the Middle East, but even bigger than that,

00:47:20.660 --> 00:47:25.660
like in 2024, how likely are you seeing at this point

00:47:25.940 --> 00:47:30.940
a broader global war, potentially World War III

00:47:31.540 --> 00:47:34.280
or something breaking out with the U.S. involved?

00:47:34.280 --> 00:47:38.000
Is it like on a scale of one to 10,

00:47:38.000 --> 00:47:40.440
where would you put it as far as, yeah,

00:47:40.440 --> 00:47:45.440
your knowledge on, is it incredibly dangerous times or?

00:47:45.720 --> 00:47:48.000
Yeah, we're in perilous times.

00:47:48.000 --> 00:47:50.520
I would put it, I think, at a six or a seven.

00:47:50.520 --> 00:47:51.360
Okay.

00:47:51.360 --> 00:47:53.840
And to me, that's pretty dangerous territory.

00:47:53.840 --> 00:47:55.980
And I think that there are several places

00:47:55.980 --> 00:47:58.480
where we should be particularly focused.

00:47:58.480 --> 00:48:00.320
First of all, I think that the Israelis

00:48:00.320 --> 00:48:02.200
are going to expand operations

00:48:02.200 --> 00:48:05.720
and that's going to be in Southern Lebanon.

00:48:05.720 --> 00:48:06.560
Okay.

00:48:06.560 --> 00:48:08.160
I think that they're going to want,

00:48:08.160 --> 00:48:10.080
once they have Gaza in hand,

00:48:10.080 --> 00:48:13.080
which I think is just a disaster for human rights.

00:48:13.080 --> 00:48:13.920
Yeah.

00:48:13.920 --> 00:48:14.740
A disaster.

00:48:16.400 --> 00:48:17.620
And we can talk about that in a second,

00:48:17.620 --> 00:48:20.360
but I think once the Israelis complete the,

00:48:21.280 --> 00:48:23.160
I hate to use this horrible cold word,

00:48:23.160 --> 00:48:25.760
but the pacification of Gaza.

00:48:25.760 --> 00:48:26.600
Yeah.

00:48:26.600 --> 00:48:28.420
I think they're going to turn their attention

00:48:28.420 --> 00:48:30.120
to his bala again.

00:48:30.120 --> 00:48:33.400
And I think that the Lebanese are worried about this.

00:48:33.400 --> 00:48:36.000
Remember, his bala now is a legitimate political party

00:48:36.000 --> 00:48:36.840
in Lebanon.

00:48:36.840 --> 00:48:37.680
Okay.

00:48:37.680 --> 00:48:39.400
It's actually one of the governmental leaders

00:48:39.400 --> 00:48:41.120
in the Lebanese government.

00:48:41.120 --> 00:48:44.000
And so, his bala has a lot more to lose now

00:48:44.000 --> 00:48:46.080
than it did 20 years ago.

00:48:46.080 --> 00:48:50.400
So that's why we haven't seen whole scale attacks

00:48:50.400 --> 00:48:52.800
across the border from Lebanon into Israel.

00:48:52.800 --> 00:48:55.960
There have been these pinprick rocket launches

00:48:56.040 --> 00:48:58.680
at Israeli bases

00:48:58.680 --> 00:49:02.240
and at a couple of the Israeli settlements up north.

00:49:02.240 --> 00:49:03.720
But I think it's going to be the Israelis

00:49:03.720 --> 00:49:05.440
that are going to be the aggressors there.

00:49:05.440 --> 00:49:07.400
So that's number one.

00:49:07.400 --> 00:49:10.360
Number two, where I see the US getting involved

00:49:11.600 --> 00:49:16.600
is with or against the Houthis in Yemen.

00:49:17.120 --> 00:49:17.960
Okay.

00:49:17.960 --> 00:49:22.080
The Houthis are seriously playing with fire right now.

00:49:22.080 --> 00:49:24.680
They're actually sending like drones

00:49:24.680 --> 00:49:29.680
and somehow already harassing our ships, right?

00:49:30.320 --> 00:49:34.000
Drones, cruise missiles and ballistic anti-ship missiles.

00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:34.840
Okay.

00:49:34.840 --> 00:49:38.520
But we're recording this on the 10th of January.

00:49:38.520 --> 00:49:39.360
Yeah.

00:49:39.360 --> 00:49:44.040
Yesterday on the 9th, they launched 18 suicide drones,

00:49:44.040 --> 00:49:46.400
two anti-ship cruise missiles

00:49:46.400 --> 00:49:48.400
and one anti-ship ballistic missile

00:49:49.320 --> 00:49:53.760
at US and British warships in the Red Sea.

00:49:53.760 --> 00:49:55.480
We knocked all of them out of the sky.

00:49:55.480 --> 00:49:56.320
Right?

00:49:56.320 --> 00:49:57.160
Yeah.

00:49:57.160 --> 00:50:00.200
Nothing hit a target, but you can't.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:03.520
poke the hornet's nest and not expect to be stung.

00:50:03.520 --> 00:50:05.920
I understand what the Houthis are doing,

00:50:05.920 --> 00:50:10.160
and some people might say it's kind of noble or heroic.

00:50:10.160 --> 00:50:12.640
They're trying to disrupt shipping

00:50:12.640 --> 00:50:17.040
so that it adversely affects the Israeli economy.

00:50:17.040 --> 00:50:20.760
The problem is that almost none of the ships

00:50:20.760 --> 00:50:23.720
they've attacked have anything to do with Israel.

00:50:23.720 --> 00:50:24.560
Yeah.

00:50:24.560 --> 00:50:25.400
Right?

00:50:25.400 --> 00:50:32.880
You can't hijack a ship, pirate a ship on the high seas,

00:50:32.880 --> 00:50:39.400
force it into port in Aden, and hold as hostage two dozen sailors

00:50:39.400 --> 00:50:44.720
from the Philippines, Bangladesh, Malaysia, Vietnam,

00:50:44.720 --> 00:50:46.560
and say, oh, we did it in solidarity

00:50:46.560 --> 00:50:48.760
with the Palestinian people.

00:50:48.760 --> 00:50:50.320
What are you talking about?

00:50:50.320 --> 00:50:51.800
Yeah.

00:50:51.800 --> 00:50:54.120
And then when the US, it's not just the US.

00:50:54.120 --> 00:50:56.920
There are six allied countries now that have warships

00:50:56.920 --> 00:50:59.600
in the Red Sea to protect shipping,

00:50:59.600 --> 00:51:03.240
and then you launch 18 suicide drones against the US Navy

00:51:03.240 --> 00:51:05.800
and you don't expect to be retaliated against?

00:51:05.800 --> 00:51:07.480
Are you out of your minds?

00:51:07.480 --> 00:51:10.560
And are the Houthis actually representative

00:51:10.560 --> 00:51:13.360
of the Yemen government, or are they?

00:51:13.360 --> 00:51:15.480
That's kind of the $64,000 question.

00:51:15.480 --> 00:51:16.240
OK.

00:51:16.240 --> 00:51:21.000
And now they control the government.

00:51:21.000 --> 00:51:21.800
OK.

00:51:21.840 --> 00:51:25.200
But the control that the Houthis have

00:51:25.200 --> 00:51:30.440
is largely just the city of Sana'a and northern Yemen.

00:51:30.440 --> 00:51:31.560
OK.

00:51:31.560 --> 00:51:34.200
What used to be called Pidri, the People's

00:51:34.200 --> 00:51:37.240
Democratic Republic of Yemen, or South Yemen,

00:51:37.240 --> 00:51:41.640
it's kind of a no-man's land except for the city of Aden.

00:51:41.640 --> 00:51:42.440
OK.

00:51:42.440 --> 00:51:47.280
The rest is just, there's an area called the Hadramut,

00:51:47.280 --> 00:51:51.160
which is, it's funny, Hadramut comes from two Arabic

00:51:51.160 --> 00:51:53.640
words, Khadr, which means vegetation,

00:51:53.640 --> 00:51:57.600
and Malt, which means dead or death.

00:51:57.600 --> 00:52:01.840
Because it's so dry there that it doesn't even have animals.

00:52:01.840 --> 00:52:02.320
Right?

00:52:02.320 --> 00:52:04.920
Like desert foxes like you see in Sana'a,

00:52:04.920 --> 00:52:07.520
there's just nothing can live there.

00:52:07.520 --> 00:52:10.400
That area is controlled by al-Qaeda.

00:52:10.400 --> 00:52:11.640
OK.

00:52:11.640 --> 00:52:15.560
The country's all divided up into these warring factions,

00:52:15.560 --> 00:52:21.200
but the Houthis control more of it than anybody else does.

00:52:21.200 --> 00:52:22.280
OK.

00:52:22.280 --> 00:52:25.760
And what are the diplomatic ties then?

00:52:25.760 --> 00:52:31.280
Obviously, Hezbollah has strong ties to Iran.

00:52:31.280 --> 00:52:31.800
OK.

00:52:31.800 --> 00:52:35.200
So, and that is basically the big concern

00:52:35.200 --> 00:52:38.360
about escalation, correct, is Iran?

00:52:38.360 --> 00:52:41.800
At five separate times over the last 20 years,

00:52:41.800 --> 00:52:44.000
Benjamin Netanyahu has approached

00:52:44.040 --> 00:52:46.880
four different American presidents

00:52:46.880 --> 00:52:50.000
and has asked us to bomb Iran.

00:52:50.000 --> 00:52:50.840
Yeah.

00:52:50.840 --> 00:52:54.560
And every time we've said no, we don't have a beef

00:52:54.560 --> 00:52:56.960
with the Iranians to the point where we're

00:52:56.960 --> 00:52:59.680
ready to start World War III, the Israelis

00:52:59.680 --> 00:53:01.600
are itching to bomb the Iranians.

00:53:01.600 --> 00:53:04.000
Now, the Iranians have been smart enough

00:53:04.000 --> 00:53:06.720
to not attack Israel directly.

00:53:06.720 --> 00:53:08.560
They do it with proxies, just like they

00:53:08.560 --> 00:53:11.280
attack us through proxies.

00:53:11.280 --> 00:53:17.480
Qatar, Hezbollah in Iraq, for example, Hezbollah in Lebanon,

00:53:17.480 --> 00:53:22.320
the Houthis in Yemen, they don't attack us directly.

00:53:22.320 --> 00:53:23.880
If they were to attack us directly,

00:53:23.880 --> 00:53:26.920
we would have to retaliate, and they don't want to risk it.

00:53:26.920 --> 00:53:27.480
Yeah.

00:53:27.480 --> 00:53:31.360
So it's the Israelis that I don't trust.

00:53:31.360 --> 00:53:32.680
OK.

00:53:32.680 --> 00:53:34.840
Didn't you mention in one story

00:53:34.840 --> 00:53:40.480
that when you were in, actually, as an analyst, I believe,

00:53:40.480 --> 00:53:44.520
or, well, I can't remember the content.

00:53:44.520 --> 00:53:48.480
I think it was the first Gulf War that we already,

00:53:48.480 --> 00:53:52.960
like we were debating and invading Iran at that time?

00:53:52.960 --> 00:53:55.160
Yeah, that was the Second Iraq War.

00:53:55.160 --> 00:53:56.280
Oh, yeah.

00:53:56.280 --> 00:53:57.080
OK.

00:53:57.080 --> 00:53:57.920
Yeah.

00:53:57.920 --> 00:53:59.240
Yeah.

00:53:59.240 --> 00:54:02.960
So it's, yeah, I mean, it's close, yeah.

00:54:03.000 --> 00:54:05.760
That's not unusual.

00:54:05.760 --> 00:54:10.360
Every major military on Earth has contingency plans

00:54:10.360 --> 00:54:11.840
to ensure their enemies.

00:54:11.840 --> 00:54:12.480
Yeah.

00:54:12.480 --> 00:54:15.840
And they're updated constantly as technologies change,

00:54:15.840 --> 00:54:19.840
as diplomatic relations change, as international alliances

00:54:19.840 --> 00:54:20.680
change.

00:54:20.680 --> 00:54:25.640
But yeah, we were fully prepared in 2002 to invade Iran.

00:54:25.640 --> 00:54:32.360
And is it as straightforward as, if, say, Israel

00:54:32.400 --> 00:54:36.680
